# Task CRUD API

A CRUD API built with Python, FastAPI and SQLite.

## Technologies

- Python
- FastAPI
- SQLite
- sqlite3
- Pydantic

## Features

The API supports:

- Create tasks
- Read all tasks
- Read a single task
- Update tasks
- Delete tasks

The API uses SQLite for persistent data storage.

## Why SQLite?

SQLite was chosen because it is lightweight, simple to set up, and does not require a separate database server.

The database is stored locally as a single file called:

`tasks.db`

The application automatically creates the database and `tasks` table if they do not already exist.

## Database Structure

The database contains a table called `tasks`.

| Column | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| id | INTEGER | Primary key |
| title | TEXT | Task title |
| done | BOOLEAN | Completion status |

## Example Tasks

When the database is empty, the application automatically inserts three example tasks:

- Task1
- Task2
- Task3

The example tasks are only inserted when the table contains zero rows.

## API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/` | API information |
| GET | `/health` | Health check |
| GET | `/tasks` | Get all tasks |
| GET | `/tasks/{task_id}` | Get one task |
| POST | `/tasks` | Create a task |
| PUT | `/tasks/{task_id}` | Update a task |
| DELETE | `/tasks/{task_id}` | Delete a task |

## How to Run

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone <your-repository-url>

Navigate into the project:

cd <project-folder>

Install the dependencies:

pip install -r requirements.txt

Start the FastAPI server:

uvicorn main:app --reload

The API will be available at:

http://127.0.0.1:8000

Swagger API documentation:

http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs

SQLite Database

The database file is:

tasks.db

It is automatically created when the application starts if it does not already exist.

Example SQL Query

The following query returns all tasks:

SELECT * FROM tasks;

The following query returns only completed tasks:

SELECT * FROM tasks
WHERE done = 1;